ary history & warfare\",\"Aviation & aerospace engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"f-35\",\"pierre sprey\",\"military procurement\",\"a-10\",\"fighter aircraft\"],\"quote\":\"this entertaining video of A-10 designer Pierre Sprey talking about how the new F-35 is garbage\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"n-AbPav5E5M\",\"title\":\"Bicycle Rush Hour Utrecht (Netherlands)\",\"channel\":\"BicycleDutch\",\"summary\":\"A sped-up two-minute view of morning rush hour at a busy Utrecht junction, where thousands of bicycles and buses pass each day. It illustrates a city where about a third of trips are by bike.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN links it as a vivid example of what bike-centred cities look like in debates on cars, helmets and urban design.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"dutch cycling infrastructure\",\"categories\":[\"Transit, cities & urban planning\"],\"tags\":[\"utrecht\",\"cycling\",\"urban planning\",\"bike lanes\",\"netherlands\"],\"quote\":\"Here is a nice example of a typical rush hour\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"n-BZ5-Q48lE\",\"title\":\"New NES Tetris Technique: Faster Than Hypertapping!\",\"channel\":\"aGameScout\",\"summary\":\"aGameScout explains rolling, the third major NES Tetris playstyle, in which players tap the back of the controller to move pieces faster than hypertapping. It covers how the technique works and where it comes from.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as the concise explanation of the latest competitive NES Tetris technique.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"nes tetris techniques\",\"categories\":[\"Speedrunning, glitches & game hacking\",\"Game history & retro gaming\",\"Gaming culture & analysis\"],\"tags\":[\"nes tetris\",\"rolling\",\"hypertapping\",\"competitive tetris\",\"controller technique\"],\"quote\":\"fascinating 9-minute YouTube video that explains the latest NES Tetris competitive tech\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"n