xism and Communism | Lex Fridman Podcast #295\",\"channel\":\"Lex Fridman\",\"summary\":\"Lex Fridman interviews economist Richard Wolff, a Marxist, about Marxism, communism, capitalism and worker cooperatives. The conversation runs nearly three hours.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN mentions it occasionally as a source for Wolff's views, such as on worker co-ops, rather than as a widely recommended watch.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"marxist economics\",\"categories\":[\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\",\"Philosophy & ethics\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"richard wolff\",\"marxism\",\"capitalism\",\"worker cooperatives\",\"lex fridman\"],\"quote\":null,\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"o17lBUZgjTs\",\"title\":\"The Immoral Design of Diablo Immortal\",\"channel\":\"Josh Strife Hayes\",\"summary\":\"Josh Strife Hayes critiques Diablo Immortal's monetization, arguing it is a gacha game in a Diablo skin with predatory spending mechanics.\",\"why_hn\":\"Pointed to as a breakdown of predatory monetization design in games.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"predatory game monetization\",\"categories\":[\"Game design\",\"Gaming culture & analysis\"],\"tags\":[\"diablo immortal\",\"gacha\",\"microtransactions\",\"game design\",\"mmo\"],\"quote\":\"if anyone isn't familiar with the predatory design of Diablo Immortal I'd recommend this video.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"o1dgrvlWML4\",\"title\":\"Feynman :: Rules of Chess\",\"channel\":\"defjam99b\",\"summary\":\"A three-minute clip of Richard Feynman using the rules of chess as an analogy for how science works, discovering rules by observation and sometimes meeting surprises like castling. It touches on incremental progress versus revolutions.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited in discussions of the scientific method and empiricism as Feynman's classic analogy of watching a game to infer its rules.\",\"content_type\