rics and mix them with other fabrics to create new garments\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"obS6TUVSZds\",\"title\":\"EEVblog #632 - Solar Roadways Are RUBBISH!\",\"channel\":\"EEVblog\",\"summary\":\"Dave Jones of EEVblog debunks the Solar Roadways project, which raised millions through Indiegogo and government funding. He works through the solar generation and LED power calculations to show the idea isn't viable.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as the go-to debunking whenever solar roads come up, because it does the math.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"solar roadways\",\"categories\":[\"Renewables, batteries & storage\",\"Electronics & circuit design\"],\"tags\":[\"solar power\",\"debunking\",\"engineering calculations\",\"crowdfunding\",\"energy\"],\"quote\":\"In this video he does the math.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"ofA6YWVTURU\",\"title\":\"Will Wright GDC 2005 Spore (The Future of Content) Remastered\",\"channel\":\"Zeusmonomon\",\"summary\":\"A remastered recording of Will Wright's 2005 GDC talk revealing Spore, titled The Future of Content. He covers procedurally generated content and the ambitions of the game, with gameplay demo starting around 12:30.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it for Wright's ideas on procedural design and as the source of the huge expectations around Spore.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"procedural game design\",\"categories\":[\"Game design\",\"Game programming & engines\"],\"tags\":[\"will wright\",\"spore\",\"gdc\",\"procedural generation\",\"game design\"],\"quote\":\"a talk by Will Wright on the (originally planned) procedurally generated design of Spore lives rent free in my brain\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"ohDB5gbtaEQ\",\"title\":\"Argument - Monty Python\",\"channel\":\"palestne\",\"summary\":\"The classic Monty Python 'Argument Clinic' sketch, lightly trimmed, in which a man pays for an argument and gets contradiction instead.\",\"why_hn\":\"Mostly posted as a joke reply in arguments, with one commenter recommending it as a lovely skit about how to argue.\",\"content_type\":\"comedy\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"monty python sketch\",\"categories\":[\"Stand-up & sketch comedy\"],\"tags\":[\"monty python\",\"argument clinic\",\"sketch comedy\",\"humor\"],\"quote\":\"absolutely lovely Monty python skit\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"oponIfu5L3Y\",\"title\":\"Afroman - Will You Help Me Repair My Door (OFFICIAL MUSIC VIDEO)\",\"channel\":\"ogafroman\",\"summary\":\"Afroman's music video for a song about police damaging his door, built from home security footage of an officers' raid on his house.\",\"why_hn\":\"Referenced in stories about the raid and the lawsuit as the source video, showing the footage and his response.\",\"content_type\":\"music\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"police raid music video\",\"categories\":[\"Music performance & songs\",\"Law, policing & justice\"],\"tags\":[\"afroman\",\"police raid\",\"surveillance footage\",\"lawsuit\",\"hip hop\"],\"quote\":\"It's worth watching the original video, it shows the officers damaging his property, eating his cake and doing various other questionable things\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"orQKfIXMiA8\",\"title\":\"You Need to Be Bored. Here's Why.\",\"channel\":\"Harvard Business Review\",\"summary\":\"Harvard professor Arthur Brooks explains why boredom is useful rather than something to avoid. He describes how a wandering mind engages the brain's default mode network, which supports creativity and curiosity, and suggests it may protect against depression.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters cite it when arguing for less phone time and more idle, undistracted thinking.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"boredom and attention\",\"categories\":[\"Neuroscience & the brain\",\"Productivity & self-improvement\",\"Psychology & human behavior\"],\"tags\":[\"boredom\",\"default mode network\",\"creativity\",\"phone use\",\"wellbeing\"],\"quote\":\"Curiosity kicks in. Curiosity is a precursor to learning.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"outcGtbnMuQ\",\"title\":\"GPT-4 Developer Livestream\",\"channel\":\"OpenAI\",\"summary\":\"OpenAI's livestream demo of GPT-4 with Greg Brockman, showing its capabilities and limitations. Highlights include writing code, turning a hand-drawn sketch into a website, and a tax-question example.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN refers back to it as the primary source for what GPT-4 could do at launch, especially the sketch-to-website and multimodal demos.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"gpt-4 capabilities\",\"categories\":[\"LLMs & generative AI\"],\"tags\":[\"gpt-4\",\"openai\",\"multimodal\",\"code generation\",\"greg brockman\"],\"quote\":\"the TaxGPT example in the GPT-4 Developer Livestream [1] was powerful\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"ovD0aLdRUs0\",\"title\":\"Why Can't we Remake the Rocketdyne F1 Engine?\",\"channel\":\"Curious Droid\",\"summary\":\"Short Curious Droid video on why NASA could not simply rebuild the Saturn V's Rocketdyne F-1 engine for the SLS boosters. It explains that the engines were hand-tailored and that much of the know-how was never documented, so the blueprints were not enough.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as the standard illustration of lost tacit knowledge and why old blueprints cannot be turned back into hardware.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"rocket engine history\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Mechanical & precision engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"f-1 engine\",\"saturn v\",\"tacit knowledge\",\"nasa sls\",\"apollo\"],\"quote\":\"TLDR: everything was handcrafted, notes were not made or lost\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"owGykVbfgUE\",\"title\":\"Old Spice | The Man Your Man Could Smell Like\",\"