    ",{\"vid\":\"pnmRYRRDbuw\",\"title\":\"The PewDiePipeline: how racist humor leads to violence\",\"channel\":\"NonCompete\",\"summary\":\"NonCompete's video examines the alt-right pipeline and a 'pyramid of violence' running from implicit bias through edgy racist humor to real violence. It uses the PewDiePie controversy and Charlottesville as case studies.\",\"why_hn\":\"Pointed to in radicalization threads as a good explanation of how online humor can funnel people toward extremism.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"online radicalization\",\"categories\":[\"Social issues & culture\",\"Internet culture & memes\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\"],\"tags\":[\"alt-right pipeline\",\"pewdiepie\",\"memes\",\"radicalization\",\"extremism\"],\"quote\":\"A good video which goes over this is The PewDiePieline\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"psAXMqxwol8\",\"title\":\"Inno-Versity Presents: Greatness by David Marquet\",\"channel\":\"Speakers Spotlight\",\"summary\":\"Retired submarine captain David Marquet explains, with drawings, how he turned the USS Santa Fe around by treating his crew as leaders rather than followers. It summarizes the ideas of his book Turn the Ship Around.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a short, illustrated take on empowering teams instead of giving orders.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"leadership\",\"categories\":[\"Management, leadership & organizations\",\"Ships, submarines & maritime\"],\"tags\":[\"david marquet\",\"empowerment\",\"team culture\",\"management\",\"turn the ship around\"],\"quote\":\"Also here's a great speech given by the David Marquet (with drawings!) on the same topic\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"ptjedOZEXPM\",\"title\":\"Google I/O 2008 - Dalvik Virtual Machine Internals\",\"channel\":\"Google for Developers\",\"summary\":\"Dan Bornstein's Google I/O 2008 talk on the internals of Dalvik, the virtual machine that runs Android code. It covers the motivation for its design, the dex format and its register-based interpreter, plus tips for writing code that suits the platform.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as the primary source on Dalvik's dex bytecode, register-based design and memory-saving choices.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"virtual machine internals\",\"categories\":[\"Compilers, interpreters & program analysis\",\"Operating systems & kernels\"],\"tags\":[\"dalvik\",\"android\",\"dex bytecode\",\"register-based vm\",\"google io\"],\"quote\":\"Dan Bornstein's talk at Google I/O 2008 about the dex format and the original Dalvik interpreter\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"q2gO4DKVpa8\",\"title\":\"Beware, fellow plutocrats, the pitchforks are coming | Nick Hanauer\",\"channel\":\"TED\",\"summary\":\"Billionaire Nick Hanauer warns fellow wealthy people in a TED talk that growing inequality could lead to social upheaval like pre-revolutionary France. He argues a higher minimum wage would grow the middle class and prosperity.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN brings it up in inequality, UBI and backlash threads as an early warning from a rich insider.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"economic inequality\",\"categories\":[\"Labor, work & inequality\",\"Macroeconomics & financial crises\"],\"tags\":[\"nick hanauer\",\"inequality\",\"minimum wage\",\"ted talk\",\"wealth\"],\"quote\":\"Nick Hanauer understood this fourteen years ago.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"q4TZxj-Dq7s\",\"title\":\"Why We Run FreeBSD current at Netflix – Drew Gallatin\",\"channel\":\"OpenFest Bulgaria\",\"summary\":\"Netflix engineer Drew Gallatin explains why the company runs FreeBSD-current on its CDN. He describes the team, how they track upstream, their contributions and performance milestones, and a bug causing a 20% performance regression.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as the Netflix case for staying close to -CUR