ah Rubin generated every possible melody and released them under CC0 to avoid accidental infringement claims.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as the stunt behind 'copyright every melody' in threads about music copyright, takedowns and AI authorship.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"music copyright\",\"categories\":[\"Law, policing & justice\",\"Music performance & songs\",\"Ideas & learning (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"melody copyright\",\"cc0\",\"infringement\",\"music law\",\"algorithmic generation\"],\"quote\":\"They did a great Tedx talk here\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"sLCHg9mUBag\",\"title\":\"Walt Disney's E.P.C.O.T film (1966)\",\"channel\":\"The Original EPCOT\",\"summary\":\"The 1966 film Walt Disney recorded weeks before his death, laying out his plans for the Florida Project and especially EPCOT, a planned city of the future. It uses models, concept art and animation to describe the circular city, monorails and people movers.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it in discussions of planned cities and urban design as the original source for Disney's utopian EPCOT vision.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"planned cities\",\"categories\":[\"Transit, cities & urban planning\",\"Tech company stories & documentaries\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"epcot\",\"walt disney\",\"urban planning\",\"utopia\",\"monorail\"],\"quote\":\"The full EPCOT plans are interesting.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"sLFaa6RPJIU\",\"title\":\"Making YBCO superconductor\",\"channel\":\"Applied Science\",\"summary\":\"Ben Krasnow of Applied Science shows how to make and test YBCO high-temperature superconductor with a kiln and eBay chemicals. He demonstrates flux pinning and shows a close-up of the crystal structure.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it in superconductor and LK-99 threads as evidence that YBCO can be made in a modest home lab.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"high-temperature superconductors\",\"categories\":[\"Materials science\",\"Chemistry\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\"],\"tags\":[\"ybco\",\"superconductor\",\"flux pinning\",\"diy science\",\"liquid nitrogen\"],\"quote\":\"Here's his video of making YBCO for anyone that hasn't seen it\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"sQ56ve39l2I\",\"title\":\"iPhone Air Durability test -- I AM SHOCKED\",\"channel\":\"JerryRigEverything\",\"summary\":\"JerryRigEverything puts the iPhone Air through scratch, bend and durability tests and is surprised that the ultra-thin phone proves very tough. The video is sponsored by dbrand cases.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as evidence against the assumption that thin modern phones are fragile.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"phone durability testing\",\"categories\":[\"Consumer devices & gadgets\",\"Repair, teardowns & right to repair\"],\"tags\":[\"iphone air\",\"bend test\",\"scratch test\",\"jerryrigeverything\",\"hardware\"],\"quote\":\"take a look at the latest Jerry Rig Everything video where it exceeded his typical scratch test resits and he was unable to bend it with his hands.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"sR8M4zARBXY\",\"title\":\"Synthesizing Chicken Noodle Soup From Pure Chemicals\",\"channel\":\"The Thought Emporium\",\"summary\":\"The Thought Emporium synthesizes chicken noodle soup from pure chemicals, following an original patent for artificial chicken flavor. The video explores how many chemicals it takes to make a convincing soup.\",\"why_hn\":\"Brought up in threads on synthetic food and flavor as a fun example of building a dish from chemicals.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"synthetic food chemistry\",\"categories\":[\"Chemistry\",\"Cooking & food\"],\"tags\":[\"food science\",\"artificial flavor\",\"chemical synthesis\",\"chicken soup\"],\"quote\":\"There's a great recent Thought Empo